# Insight 008 — Recency and Revenue Concentration

## Finding

Recent customers account for a disproportionate share of historical revenue.

Customers purchasing within the last 90 days represent approximately 30% of the customer base but account for more than 61% of total revenue.

Customers purchasing within the last 30 days alone represent approximately 14.4% of customers and 40.4% of revenue.

In contrast, 573 customers (29.3% of the customer base) have not purchased for more than 365 days and account for approximately 10.1% of historical revenue.

## Business Impact

Recency is strongly associated with customer economic activity and represents an important dimension for customer segmentation.

However, high recency should not automatically be interpreted as customer churn because expected purchasing cycles differ substantially between product categories.

## Recommendation

Recency should be incorporated into customer segmentation but interpreted together with historical frequency, customer value and product mix.

