# Insight 009 — Reactivation Opportunities

## Finding

Not all customers with high recency have historically low engagement.

Among customers with more than 365 days since their last recorded purchase, 79 customers had previously completed at least four purchases during the analyzed period.

This group generated approximately R$198,000 in historical revenue and R$79,000 in profit, with an average of approximately 7.9 purchases per customer.

## Business Impact

Treating all inactive customers equally would overlook meaningful differences in their previous relationship with the company.

Previously frequent customers who have stopped purchasing may represent stronger reactivation opportunities than customers with only one historical transaction.

## Recommendation

Future reactivation strategies should prioritize customers based on a combination of:

- Recency
- Historical frequency
- Revenue
- Profit
- Product mix

A dedicated "Customers to Reactivate" segment or dashboard view should be considered.

